  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "A box \\(2\\) centimeters high, \\(3\\) centimeters wide, and \\(5\\) centimeters long can hold \\(40\\) grams of clay. A second box with twice the height, three times the width, and the same length as the first box can hold \\(n\\) grams of clay. What is \\(n?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(120\\)",
    "B": "\\(160\\)",
    "C": "\\(200\\)",
    "D": "\\(240\\)",
    "E": "\\(280\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A rectangular box's volume is its length times its width times its height. Multiplying the height by \\(2\\), the width by \\(3\\), and keeping the length unchanged therefore multiplies the volume by\n\\[\n2\\cdot3\\cdot1=6.\n\\]\nFor the same clay packed in the same way, six times the volume holds six times the mass. Thus\n\\[\nn=6\\cdot40=240\n\\]\ngrams, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
